// =============================================================================
// <BRAND> — Design System Foundation
// =============================================================================
// Compiles to assets/<brand>.css, which layout/theme.liquid loads AFTER the
// vendor bundle.
//
// RULES
//   1. assets/<vendor>.css is a vendor bundle — never edit it. Everything here
//      is an override layer on top of it.
//   2. Token values are lifted verbatim from design/<file>.html:<lines> so a
//      diff against the design can be traced back one-to-one. Do not rename
//      them to a "nicer" scheme.
//   3. No !important. Where the cascade needs help, raise specificity the same
//      way the design does.
//   4. Section-specific CSS does NOT belong here — it goes in that section's
//      {% stylesheet %} block. This file is global only.
//   5. CSS round() must never be written in SCSS — Sass claims that function
//      name. Any round(down, …) pixel-snapping goes in a {% stylesheet %}
//      block, which is plain CSS.
//   6. Never scope by #shopify-section-<id> — section-group ids are generated
//      per store/theme, and no amount of classes beats an ID. Put the CSS
//      variable on the element that CONSUMES it instead.
//
// Ground truth: <baselineDir>/design-metrics-*.json
// =============================================================================
